{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1122748-gates-of-horn-and-ivory","id":1122748,"title":"Gates of Horn and Ivory","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-30T11:22:10-07:00","id":1122748,"title":"Gates of Horn and Ivory","content":"I noticed that the Gates of Horn and Ivory were mentioned in the contracts of steed preview. <br /> <br /> Any speculation on their current incarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T16:09:15-07:00","id":1122827,"title":"","content":"My speculation: They're the 'proper' way to enter a dream bastion, and how the dreamer's consciousness got inside. Going by the real world mythology, which gate you go in might determine whether you see a 'false' dream or a 'true' prophetic/psychoanalytical one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T17:30:24-07:00","id":1122856,"title":"","content":"Since &quot;true&quot; dreams were said to come through the gate of horn, I wonder if this is how changelings will dream ride in 2E. Using this gate might allow them to physically remain in Ironside, yet still observe or possibly even make minor changes to a dream without actually entering the bastion and altering it's core &quot;truth&quot;. The gate of ivory, on the other hand, was considered the origin of &quot;false&quot; dreams, so this route might be how changelings will be able to physically enter a bastion for active dreamscaping, such as engaging in oneiromachy or obtaining baubles to create hedgespun. Since they would dramatically alter the original dream with such wacky high jinks, this would turn it into a &quot;false&quot; dream. At least, this was the house rule I came up with soon after reading the original spoiler where changelings either faded from the real world or slept without dreaming. So glad that isn't a thing anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12559-hedgebound-heart","name":"Hedgebound Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}